			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add Shim module with Gate and SwallowMap for IPC interception\n\nEstablish the Rust-level foundation for the deep-shim interception layer introduced by the TierShim env-var in the prior commit. Two new modules live behind the `pub mod Shim` declaration in Library.rs:\n\n- **Gate** — Compile-time tier gate reading `env!(\"TierShim\")` (baked by build.rs via EmitTierDefaults), exporting boolean guards (`is_enabled`, `is_proxy`, `is_replace_or_deeper`, `is_own_or_preempt`, `is_preempt`) that drive `#[cfg]` gating throughout Mountain. Zero overhead at default `None` tier via dead-code elimination.\n\n- **SwallowMap** — Pattern-matching decision engine that maps IPC method names (e.g. `statusbar:`, `telemetry:`) to a `SwallowAction`/`RedirectTarget` pair, determining whether Mountain handles the call locally, forwards it to Wind/Cocoon/Output/Sky, or discards it entirely (telemetry). Rules are checked in insertion order; first match wins with a default `Passthrough → None` fallback.\n\nCargo.toml gains inline comments documenting the four active shim tiers and their corresponding Rust features. This completes the Rust-side routing infrastructure for the Land Shim plan.\n\nSee: `.hermes/microsoft/05-Mountain-Rust-Intercept.md`",
			"SHA": "d22f305e382b83b58e9a6ac5f32ce87c7369afc3"
		},
